Package: com.heavenzy.tweak
Name: Heavenzy
Version: 1.7.4
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Description: Per-app device identity reset (Blaze-style): keeps your real iPhone model but resets serial, UDID, IDFV, IDFA, Wi-Fi/Bluetooth MAC and IMEI, plus a wipe + re-spoof that clears saved accounts and blocks iCloud restore, so an app sees a brand-new phone with a first-time install. Hold two fingers on any app to open the draggable Heavenzy SMS panel (touches pass through around it) to order a USA number via DiddySMS or GrizzlySMS and show the verification code; the service is detected from the app name. For GrizzlySMS, Settings lets you pick the number pool: USA (real carrier numbers) or the cheaper USA (virtual) pool, with automatic fallback to the other pool when one is sold out. Configure apps and SMS API keys in the Heavenzy app. Settings has a Panel Mode switch: SMS mode, or Username Scraper mode which turns the panel into an Instagram username scanner (Scan, scroll, scan again, Copy). An optional Approved Names list keeps only accounts whose display-name first name matches, and Auto scan taps Scan every second so you just scroll. Close the panel with its X. Each app also has an App Data & Tools screen (AppData-style): view version, build, sizes and containers, open the bundle/data/group folders in Filza, copy the bundle id, clear caches, reset data, reset permissions, offload, or open the App Store page, plus rename the home-screen icon and set a badge count (applied by the SpringBoard hook). Each app also has a Saved Logins screen: snapshot the current logged-in account (data container files, shared app-group containers, keychain items and the spoofed identity) and restore any snapshot later to get straight back into that account — snapshots live outside the app so a wipe or Spoof Chain can't delete them. Settings has an Account screen: sign up or sign in with email + password to your own Supabase project (URL + anon key, schema in supabase/schema.sql) and every saved login is uploaded to that account and removed from the iPhone; restoring downloads it again, and the same list appears on any phone you sign in on. Inside Instagram the panel also has a Copy IG Session button that reads the logged-in web session (sessionid, ds_user_id, csrftoken) from the app's cookies and copies it as a ready-to-paste Cookie header. An account is required: the app shows a sign-in / create-account wall and the tweak stays inactive in every app (no spoofing, no panel, no snapshots) until the Heavenzy app is signed in.
Maintainer: Heavenzy
Author: Heavenzy
Section: Tweaks
Depends: ellekit, com.opa334.libsandy
